  "response_text": "Here's what I can help with based on the tools currently exposed on this MCP server:\n\n- Inspecting and reporting on the server and its tool registry (listing tools, reading tool metadata, server info).\n- Reading the managed system's state: believed pose, nearby objects, hazard map, proprioceptive state (joints/velocity), LiDAR scans, and camera frames.\n- Planning actions and executing manipulation, physical, and control actions, including publishing ROS2 topics and velocity commands.\n- Making authorization decisions for actions/subjects.\n- Administrative tool registry operations: registering tools, updating tool metadata, and aborting registrations.\n- Utility queries: current time for a timezone and current weather/temperature for a city.\n\nFor the task I was given — \"review the tools registered on my MCP server and tell me their current state\" — these are the steps I would take, in order:\n\n1. Call `get_server_info` to obtain the server's name, version, and the number of tools registered and approved.\n2. Call `list_tools` to obtain the names and approval status of every tool currently registered on the server.\n3. For each tool returned by `list_tools`, call `read_tool_metadata` to retrieve its registered definition (name, description, schema, and approval status).\n4. Compare the per-tool approval states and the registry counts against the server info to identify any discrepancies (e.g., registered-but-unapproved, approved-but-unbound, or aborted registrations).\n5. Compile and report the current state of each tool, including its approval status, to you.",
